\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {25}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Tract-level price event study (fig.\ T1)} The Treated coefficient is the post$-$pre effect from a single LP-DiD regression via pre-mean differencing (Dube, Girardi, Jord\`a and Taylor 2023): dependent variable $\frac  {1}{4}\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{h=0}^{3} y_{t+h} - \frac  {1}{4}\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{\tau =t-4}^{t-1} y_{\tau }$ on treatment entry with calendar-time effects, clean-control sample; its SE, $R^2$ and Observations come from that regression. Coefficients are 100$\times $log points (shares in pp). SEs clustered by unit (cell/tract). Statistical significance levels are indicated as follows: *** $p < 0.01$, ** $p < 0.05$, * $p < 0.10$.}}{25}{}\protected@file@percent }
